    "slides": [
      {
        "index": 1,
        "text": "At forty, sorting old boxes, you find a faded envelope with your father's rejected 1984 art school application.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "LIGHT",
        "logo_tone": "LIGHT",
        "footer_tone": "CHARCOAL",
        "accent": "GOLD"
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "text": "This was the same man who insisted throughout your youth that creative pursuits were foolish and security was everything.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "LIGHT",
        "logo_tone": "LIGHT",
        "footer_tone": "CHARCOAL",
        "accent": "GOLD"
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "text": "For decades, his strict advice felt like a dismissal of your early interests, a boundary meant to narrow your options.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "LIGHT",
        "logo_tone": "LIGHT",
        "footer_tone": "CHARCOAL",
        "accent": "GOLD"
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "text": "Holding those drawings, you realize his lesson was never a lack of belief in you, but his own unhealed disappointment.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "LIGHT",
        "logo_tone": "LIGHT",
        "footer_tone": "CHARCOAL",
        "accent": "GOLD"
      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "text": "Family rules are frequently constructed over the remains of an unhealed risk, designed to protect us from the specific grief they carried alone.",
        "closing": true,
        "text_tone": "LIGHT",
        "logo_tone": "LIGHT",
        "footer_tone": "CHARCOAL",
        "accent": "GOLD"
      }
    ]
  },
